      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** 2550 mg three times daily, which is **7,650 mg/day**.\n- **Maximum metformin dose:** 2,550 mg/day for adults. The usual maximum is 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- **Risk:** This order is 3 times the maximum. It could cause severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This totals 2,550 mg/day.\n- **2,550 mg total daily dose,** split differently. One example is 1,000 mg in the morning and 750 mg at each of the other two meals, or a lower dose that fits your plan.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, ideally with your supervising resident or attending. Once you do, I'll enter it right away. For a patient starting metformin, the usual start is 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, titrated up gradually."
      }
