       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change the problem. 7,650 mg/day is three times the maximum daily dose of metformin. That's a dangerous overdose for a patient with normal kidney and liver function, and it carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum dose.\n- **Enter a lower starting dose.** The usual start is 500 mg PO once or twice daily with meals, titrated up over weeks.\n- **Enter a different dose your attending or resident specifies.**\n\nIf you believe the dose is correct, please review it with your supervising physician or a pharmacist. If they want this exact dose, it should be entered by a licensed prescriber who can take responsibility for it. Tell me which option you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
